<%/* Inter and Poppins, self-hosted (static/fonts/, SIL OFL — licences alongside).

   These used to be a <link rel="stylesheet"> to fonts.googleapis.com in the head: render-
   blocking, on a host nothing else used, which then pulled the font files from a SECOND
   host (fonts.gstatic.com). Lighthouse mobile put ~850ms of first paint on it, 18 Oct
   2026. Now the @font-face rules are inline (no request at all) and the files are
   same-origin, behind assetUrl()'s year-long cache.

   Copied from what Google served for Inter:wght@400;600;700 and Poppins:wght@600;700,
   latin and latin-ext subsets only (the cyrillic/greek/vietnamese ones are never used
   here). Inter is Google's variable font: one file covers every weight, but it is
   declared at 400, 600 and 700 only, exactly as Google did. A range ("400 700") would
   render the stylesheet's four font-weight: 500 rules as true medium, where they have
   always matched the 400 face — the homepage headings would quietly get bolder. The
   browser fetches the shared file once. Poppins is one static file per weight. The unicode-ranges are
   Google's, so a browser only fetches latin-ext when a page has such a character.

   The two latin files are preloaded: Poppins 700 is the page heading (the LCP element on
   most pages) and Inter is all body text. Not latin-ext — most pages never need it.
   test/webfonts.test.js pins this. */%>
<link rel="preload" href="<%= assetUrl('/static/fonts/poppins-700-latin.woff2') %>" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" href="<%= assetUrl('/static/fonts/inter-latin.woff2') %>" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url(<%= assetUrl('/static/fonts/inter-latin-ext.woff2') %>) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C4, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url(<%= assetUrl('/static/fonts/inter-latin-ext.woff2') %>) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C4, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url(<%= assetUrl('/static/fonts/inter-latin-ext.woff2') %>) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C4, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;
  }
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url(<%= assetUrl('/static/fonts/inter-latin.woff2') %>) format('woff2');
    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
  }
